Kind: widen
Issue: #923
Holds open: unsynchronised TSCs -- the monotonic clock's reading takes the TSC 5 ms further on per processor number, so two processors' readings of one moment differ by up to a tick: the clock must still never go back
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Note: preemption is off around the reading, so that the number is that of the processor whose TSC is read; the first version read cpu_number() with it on, and the #626 check said WRONG in every boot of the A/B, the fixed tree's included.  Over it the fixed tree passed 4 of 4 at 961a96ce on omen, TCG and KVM, with no #626 report

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/time/clock_dev.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/time/clock_dev.c
index 31854f3b..f29206c5 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/time/clock_dev.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/time/clock_dev.c
@@ -56,6 +56,8 @@
 #include <kern/time_out.h>		/* tick -- microseconds per tick */
 #include <x86_64/time/tsc.h>		/* rdtsc, tsc_hz -- the sub-tick ruler */
 #include <x86_64/sync/atomic.h>		/* atomic_cmpxchg64 -- the monotonic clock's floor */
+#include <x86_64/cpu_number.h>		/* 923-widen-tsc-skew */
+#include <kern/cpu_data.h>		/* 923-widen-tsc-skew: disable_preemption */
 
 /*
  * ⚠️ <sys/time.h> is deliberately not included, although it is where the rest
@@ -453,7 +455,13 @@ mono_gettime(tvalspec_t *cur_time)
 		anchor = mono_tsc;
 		__asm__ __volatile__("" ::: "memory");
 	} while (mono_seq != seq);
-	ns = base + wall_subtick_nsec(anchor);
+	/* 923-widen-tsc-skew: each processor reads the TSC 5 ms further on per
+	 * processor number, as unsynchronised TSCs would -- with preemption off,
+	 * so that the number is that of the processor whose TSC is read */
+	disable_preemption();
+	ns = base + wall_subtick_nsec(anchor - (uint64_t) cpu_number() *
+				       (tsc_hz() / 200));
+	enable_preemption();
 
 	/* Never below what any processor has been given. */
 	given = mono_given;
